# tsshd is the server half of tssh (trzsz-ssh). rootshell on the phone connects
# with tssh, which logs in over normal SSH and then starts a tsshd process for
# the session. The session then runs over UDP, so it survives a locked phone, a
# sleeping network, and a change of IP address. tmux control mode works over
# tssh, but it does not work over mosh. There is no daemon to run: tsshd starts
# on demand, one process for each session.
brew "tsshd"
brew "homebrew-app"
